more another conditional output.

00:11:30.880 --> 00:11:32.190
Um

00:11:32.200 --> 00:11:34.110
I've drawn the same as No, we've got a

00:11:34.120 --> 00:11:37.270
loop again. So, we start in state

00:11:37.280 --> 00:11:39.110
01. We've got our state bits. We've got

00:11:39.120 --> 00:11:42.590
three outputs. LED 2 active high is a

00:11:42.600 --> 00:11:44.350
conditional output.

00:11:44.360 --> 00:11:47.390
That will go high as soon as if we stay

00:11:47.400 --> 00:11:49.150
if we're in state

00:11:49.160 --> 00:11:50.190
A

00:11:50.200 --> 00:11:52.430
which is where we start

00:11:52.440 --> 00:11:54.510
and we stay in state A as long as Z of L

00:11:54.520 --> 00:11:56.150
is

00:11:56.160 --> 00:11:59.110
high cuz it's active false. So, on the

00:11:59.120 --> 00:12:01.150
first clock edge we stay in state A

00:12:01.160 --> 00:12:03.750
because Z of L is active false. Nothing

00:12:03.760 --> 00:12:08.710
We we assert C and T and R and and uh

00:12:08.720 --> 00:12:11.470
these two signals are deasserted. So,

00:12:11.480 --> 00:12:14.910
as I said as soon as Z of L changes LED

00:12:14.920 --> 00:12:16.870
2 goes high.

00:12:16.880 --> 00:12:19.670
It will then go low on the clock edge

00:12:19.680 --> 00:12:21.310
the next clock edge because we've

00:12:21.320 --> 00:12:24.270
deasserted Z of L. So, Z of L causes

00:12:24.280 --> 00:12:27.350
causes to go high. Next clock edge

00:12:27.360 --> 00:12:29.390
we go to state B.

00:12:29.400 --> 00:12:31.870
State B doesn't list LED 2, so it goes

00:12:31.880 --> 00:12:33.390
low.

00:12:33.400 --> 00:12:35.070
And of course we assert the state

00:12:35.080 --> 00:12:36.350
output.

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:37.910
So, that's just another example showing

00:12:37.920 --> 00:12:40.630
how we can have an output active for a

00:12:40.640 --> 00:12:43.750
very short time.

00:12:43.760 --> 00:12:46.150
Uh it is conventional and and quite

00:12:46.160 --> 00:12:48.829
convenient to show the causal nature of

00:12:48.839 --> 00:12:51.510
changes in signals by an arrow. So, here

00:12:51.520 --> 00:12:52.670
in the diagram when you're drawing these

00:12:52.680 --> 00:12:54.670
